America has celebrated Memorial Day for  at least 150 years it's a post-civil war  holiday that used to be called  decoration day the name morphed over  time as the holiday grew post-world War  one to commemorate all who have died in  service to the country remembering our  fallen soldiers is more than nostalgia  it's about we engaging with the  principles that define America because  Memorial Day renews the memory of those  who gave their lives that this nation  might live  it reminds us that our nation is  dedicated to liberty and equality our  national cemeteries at Arlington and  elsewhere make it a point to specify the  individual names of fallen soldiers on  those rows on rows of headstones to  recognize the equal worthiness of each  of its dead soldiers to be remembered by  name not all democracies have done this  nation Athens dead soldiers were  nameless because it was only the city of  Athens that was meant to be remembered  it matters how a government thinks of  and treats its military dead because it  reveals how it thinks about citizens and  government do you think Americans have  lost sight of the meaning of Memorial  Day let us know in your comments also  let us know what other topics you'd like  our scholars to cover in 60 seconds and  be sure to LIKE and subscribe for more  research and videos from AEI
 

